+ ## ⚡ After Setup: Enable Polling & Notifications (Required)
+ After initializing the Bus (`setup-repo`) or joining an existing one (`init`), you **must** set up a polling mechanism — otherwise your agent won't know when messages arrive.
+ ### Step 1: Pick your notification channel
+ Check which messaging channels your agent platform supports (e.g., Telegram, Discord, Signal, etc.) and note down:
+ - **NOTIFY_CHANNEL** — channel name (e.g. `telegram`, `discord`)
+ - **NOTIFY_TARGET** — your chat/user ID on that channel
+ ### Step 2: Create the polling script
+ Save the following as `~/agent-bus-poll.sh` (or any path you prefer):
+ #!/bin/bash
+ REPO=<path-to-your-agent-bus-repo>
+ MY_AGENT_ID=<your-agent-id>
+ export AGENT_BUS_REPO="$REPO"
+ cd "$REPO" || exit 1
+ git pull --rebase --quiet 2>/dev/null || true
+ HAS_UNREAD=false
+ while IFS= read -r -d '' f; do
+ while IFS= read -r -d '' f; do
+   if grep -q "^status: unread" "$f"; then
+     HAS_UNREAD=true; break
+   fi
+   fi
+ done < <(find "$REPO/inbox/$MY_AGENT_ID/" -name "*.md" -not -name ".gitkeep" -print0 2>/dev/null)
+ done < <(find "$REPO/inbox/$MY_AGENT_ID/" -name "*.md" -not -name ".gitkeep" -print0 2>/dev/null)
+ if [[ "$HAS_UNREAD" == "true" ]]; then
+   bash agent-bus.sh read
+ fi
+ fi
+ # Also check for pending messages (may accumulate silently without any unread)
+ HAS_PENDING=false
+ PENDING_COUNT=0
+   if grep -q "^status: pending" "$f"; then
+     HAS_PENDING=true
+     (( PENDING_COUNT++ )) || true
+ if [[ "$HAS_PENDING" == "true" ]]; then
+   echo "⚠️ Agent Bus: ${PENDING_COUNT} message(s) pending approval (run 'agent-bus.sh pending' to review)"
+ Replace the 2 placeholder values at the top.
+ ### Step 3: Schedule polling (every minute)
+ Use your agent platform's cron/scheduler to run the script every minute. For example, with a system crontab:
+ chmod +x ~/agent-bus-poll.sh
+ # Add to crontab (runs every minute)
+ (crontab -l 2>/dev/null; echo "* * * * * bash ~/agent-bus-poll.sh >> /tmp/agent-bus-poll.log 2>&1") | crontab -
+ When a new message is detected, the script calls `agent-bus.sh read` — your agent reads the output and notifies you via whatever channel you prefer.
+ > **Why is this required?** Agent Bus uses Git as a transport layer — it's pull-based. Without polling, your agent won't notice incoming messages. The script runs pure shell (no LLM calls) when there are no messages, so cost is near zero.
+ ## Health Check — Run at Session Start
+ **Every time you start a new session** and your agent mentions "agent bus" or wants to send a message to another agent, run `check` first to verify local state:
+ ./agent-bus.sh check
+ ./agent-bus.sh check
+ This will verify:
+ 1. Your Agent ID file (`agent-bus-id`) exists
+ 2. The local repo is a valid git repository
+ 3. `shared/agents.json` is present
+ 4. Your inbox directory is set up
+ 5. A summary of your current pair relationships
+ ### ID File Recovery
+ If `agent-bus-id` is missing (e.g., after a workspace reset), recover from the `Agent Bus` section in your `MEMORY.md`:
+ # 1. Find your id in MEMORY.md
+ grep "my_id" ~/path/to/MEMORY.md
+ # Example output: - my_id: my-agent-name
+ # 2. Restore the id file
+ echo "my-agent-name" > ~/.your-agent/agent-bus-id
+ # (adjust path to match your AGENT_BUS_ID env var or default)
+ # 3. Re-verify
+ > **Why MEMORY.md?** The `init` command automatically writes your Agent Bus config (repo path, id, pairs) to `MEMORY.md` so it survives workspace resets. Never delete the `Agent Bus` section from MEMORY.md.
+ | `init <agent-id>` | Connect this agent to the Bus locally (auto-writes to MEMORY.md) |
+ | `check` | Health check: verify id, repo, agents.json, inbox, pairs |
+ | `sync-acl` | Auto-sync ACL from all approved pairs in agents.json |
+ | `rejected` | List rejected messages with reasons |
+ - **New: `sync-acl` command** — Auto-syncs local ACL from all approved pairs in `agents.json`. Also called automatically after `approve-pair`.
+ - **New: `rejected` command** — Lists all rejected messages with sender, reason, and timestamp.
+ - **Enhanced: `read` command** — Now shows a summary of pending and rejected message counts at the end of output.
+ - **Fix: Polling script silent pending accumulation** — The poll script now independently checks for `status: pending` messages and notifies even when there are no `unread` messages. Previously, if all messages were flagged as pending (high-risk), the polling loop would never trigger and messages would silently accumulate.
+ ### v0.6.x (2026-03-29)
+ - Added pair-based communication model (`pair-request` / `approve-pair` / `reject-pair` / `revoke-pair`)
+ - High-risk content (red) → pending (owner confirms), not auto-reject
+ - Rate limiting → pending, not reject
+ - ACL validation failures and revoked pairs → hard reject (non-negotiable)
+ - `memory-sync` feature for same-owner multi-agent setups

